&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Compatibility Issues and How to Install:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Mod has been tested on TOTK v.1.2.1, but other versions shouldn't be an&#13;
issue.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
If you use several mods editing music, you might want to disable them&#13;
especially if they edit the same tracks. &lt;b&gt;It is not recommended to have&#13;
several of them on, since the sound can be messed-up, or the files can have&#13;
priority issues. Proceed at your own risk. &lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
If you don't like one of the swapped tracks or prefer the vanilla version,&lt;b&gt; feel&#13;
free to delete both the .bwav file AND the associated .bars file from the mod's&#13;
folder&lt;/b&gt;! Default music will return normally unless you use another music&#13;
mod. &lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Manually: Download the archive and extract it, then drag the mod into your Mod&#13;
Directory. &lt;br&gt;TKMM: For the TKMM installation, open TKMM and drop the archive directly into&#13;
your mod list (without extracting). It should get installed, once done merge&#13;
your mods and save the changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Update 1.1.0 or above&lt;/b&gt;: If you have downloaded the 1.0.0 version of the mod, please delete it entirely from your Mod directory before downloading the new one. Don't attempt to replace/merge the new files with the old ones, almost all of them were reworked. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;b&gt;Patch Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.1.0: &lt;/b&gt;Overhaul of the entire soundtrack. Lowering the volume of songs so they sound less aggressive and removal of fading/silence effects to help correct looping. Added Game Over, Gerudo Underground, Lost Woods, and Flight Minigame. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.2.0&lt;/strong&gt;: Numerous additions! 22 new songs have been added, because the multi-channel issue has been thankfully solved! The Yiga Minigame song has been updated with a new one, and Dragonhead Island song has been corrected (volume and looping). I'm proud to announce this is a huge step-up!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Notes and Known Issues:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Loud tracks and janky transitions have been solved with the 1.1.0 patch! &lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Many thanks to Porroman420 for having suggested using another patching tool!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If there are any bugged tracks or a failed conversion (for ex, an in-game&#13;
track that would sound distorted, a track playing twice at once or obnoxiously&#13;
loud), please report them to me and I'll try to fix it ASAP. Don't hesitate to delete them if they&#13;
bother you. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Due to Gamebanana's file weight limit, I had to reduce the length of a lot of the new songs in 1.2.0 (mostly the battle ones) and remove the Ancient Zora Waterworks entirely (this track alone weighs a lot because it has 8 channels!) Which can result in tracks ending a bit abruptly, even if I tried my best to preserve the mod's quality. &lt;br&gt;You can find the original/uncut version on my Nexus page &lt;a href="https://www.nexusmods.com/legendofzeldatearsofthekingdom/mods/178"&gt;(The Legend of Nostalgia)&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br&gt;Apologies for the inconvenience! &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
